Hi Igor,

SIZE_E_1 stays at 0 and the diff stays as it is. Your reason is better than the
one I would have given: a register built from the trace with one field swapped
to upstream's value is a configuration nothing has ever run, and that is worth
more than a smaller diff.

Your question has an answer and it is partly uncomfortable, so let me give the
measurement rather than the summary. Since we last spoke I swept SIZE_E_2 across
all eight of its values on a second path, the int4 one, at 64 output channels:

    SIZE_E_2   0    1    2    3    4..7
    channels   32   32   36   40   the job hangs

So on that path the field is additive in FOURS, not in sixteens. That does not
sit well with the semantics I sent you on the 17th, where SIZE_E_n + 1 counted
16-channel atoms. It is a different register value on a different precision, so
it does not refute the reading for the path it was read from, and I am not going
to pretend it supports it either.

SIZE_E_1 on that path is inert: setting it from 1 to 0 leaves the channel count
at 40 and the probe's sixteen point window unchanged. That is a smaller claim
than "no effect" and it is the size of what I actually read. SIZE_E_0 is inert at
0 and hangs at 2 and at 6. RGP_CNTER and OD_BYPASS are inert, RESERVED_0 hangs.

Now the part your question actually asks, and the honest answer is that I have
not run it. I do have a channel count sweep now, seven values, 16 through 64 in
steps of 8, and every one of them ran with 0x4050 at its traced value. I have
never crossed the two. Whether some N leans on SIZE_E_1 where 64 does not is
exactly what a sweep of SIZE_E_1 AT each of those seven N would say, and it is
cheap, so it goes in the next board round rather than into a paragraph of
reasoning.

Which means your conservative choice and the honest one are the same choice for
a second reason: two shapes cannot rule it out, and I now know that seven shapes
have not been asked either.

One other thing from the same seven point sweep, since it bears on how that
register family is read. When the channel register asks for exactly n, the
hardware writes floor(n/16)*16 of them, at every one of the seven, and asking for
the next multiple of sixteen delivers all n. So sixteen is a real quantum on this
block, which is at least consistent with 16-channel atoms being the unit SIZE_E
counts something in, even if the count itself came out in fours.

The re-run offer is noted and I will take it when v9 goes. Glad the trip was
fine, and I hope the countryside is treating the board well.

Regards,
Jiaxing
